WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.647
The first CTE performs representation normalization.

00:00:03.647 --> 00:00:06.687
It does not yet claim that the values are valid.

00:00:06.687 --> 00:00:09.137
Names are cleaned for whitespace.

00:00:09.137 --> 00:00:11.662
Emails are trimmed and lowercased.

00:00:11.662 --> 00:00:14.912
Phone values become digit-only candidates.

00:00:14.912 --> 00:00:18.397
The raw signup date is carried forward unchanged.

00:00:18.397 --> 00:00:22.122
This separation makes the pipeline easier to reason about.

00:00:22.122 --> 00:00:28.697
Connect this idea to a product catalog standardizing categories and quarantining invalid rows.

00:00:28.697 --> 00:00:34.402
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:34.402 --> 00:00:41.792
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:41.792 --> 00:00:47.237
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:47.237 --> 00:00:52.720
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
